Z||000000||Bugsy||02-04-2000||04:09 PM||||Well guys I finally got my settlement check from the insurance company, I'm looking to buy some aftermarket wheels. Anyone have any recomendations?...I've looked around locally, none of the tire stores in my city have anything that grabs me unless they're $400 or better, I'm loking to spend about $150 per preferable 15" or even 16"....TIA||||reg||9
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-04-2000||04:53 PM||||If your looking for light weight... Kosei makes a (K1) 6 spoke super-light (16x8) they weigh in at like 10lbs. <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>  stuff a nice 225-50 Yokohama AVS Intermediate on them and handle like the Ferrari it was modled after. (www.discounttiredirect.com) for the tires. the Konig GT-Rs i just sold now retail for about $120 each (17x7.5) tires are about the same price. (from $100.. up) ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-06-2000||05:54 PM||||Everyone seems to like something a little different.  My wife and I were getting her tire fixed this weekend and she saw a wheel ($300/each!) that she just loved.  I happen to think it's just about the ugliest wheel I've ever seen.  On the other hand, I saw a wheel that I was interested in (much cheaper) that she thought was generic.  Look at different websites, ask alot of questions, go to tire shops, then make up your own mind.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bugsy||02-06-2000||07:41 PM||||Thanx guys, I found a set I like but of course its a discontinued style, i'll keep looking around<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000004||batboy||02-06-2000||08:12 PM||||How you tried looking at the Tire Rack website? They have a handy little doohickey that allows you to bring up an image of your type of car (they have a Fiero, but it's only in red), then you can put on any of the available wheels they sell that fits to help find the ones you like.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2FAST4U||02-06-2000||08:33 PM||||I recently bought Team Loco 142s 16X7 from Tire Rack. mounted Firestone 225ZR50 SZ50s on the for my 85 GT. They look good and fit well. Two day shipping from Tire Rack is only $8.95 extra.||||reg||1
Z||000006||tiacPaul||02-06-2000||09:40 PM||||Three spoke look bad-ass on Fieros!  That's what I'll be looking for!<BR>||||reg||6
